"""Narrative of the loop-17 report. sections(g) gets the globals of build_loop17_report.py (accessors S, bs, f3, tables, figure) and returns the html blocks.
Every number that can change is read from results_master.json through the accessors; numbers that come from a single log line are marked in the text of the table they sit in."""
import html

esc = html.escape


def sections(g):
    S, bs, f3, figure, table = g["S"], g["bs"], g["f3"], g["figure"], g["table"]
    MJ, PERT3, PERT4, NAME = g["MJ"], g["PERT3"], g["PERT4"], g["NAME"]
    has = lambda p, k: k in MJ["perts"][p]["cards"]

    def rs(tag, ph="fail", sig="0"):
        c = MJ["route"].get(tag, {})
        xs = [v["route_success"] for k, v in c.items() if k.startswith(f"sigma{sig}_") and k.endswith(f"_{ph}")]
        return sum(xs) / len(xs) if xs else float("nan")

    h = []
    cl = S("dark", "champ_single", "cl")
    cl_ctrl = S("dark", "ctrl_single", "cl")

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ title and summary
    h.append("<h1>Loop 17: the lane-graph chain under sensor failure</h1>")
    h.append("<div class='sub'>Robustness, temporal fusion and map assignment of the fully differentiable chain (camera + radar foundation, sparse lane-graph builder, route head, planner consumer) &middot; validation scenes only, test frames not touched &middot; 2026-10-24 / 25</div>")
    h.append("<h2>Summary</h2>")
    h.append(f"""<div class='box'><p><b>Question.</b> The loop-16 champion is the end-to-end candidate: a sparse lane graph (14 vertices per 100 m, 31 ms) that carries a navigation attribute into a planner. It had never been tested where a real vehicle needs it: when a sensor fails. This loop tests it on 22 validation scenes in which the second half of every scene is perturbed (night, motion blur, three front cameras off, and four milder types), and asks what temporal memory, training and the SD map can bring back.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>The failure is a loss of input, not of the builder.</b> The champion falls from S {f3(cl)} on the clean half to {f3(S('dark','champ_single'))} (night), {f3(S('blur','champ_single'))} (blur) and {f3(S('cam_front3_off','champ_single'))} (three front cameras off), as the control does ({f3(S('dark','ctrl_single'))}, {f3(S('blur','ctrl_single'))}, {f3(S('cam_front3_off','ctrl_single'))}). Lanes found drop from {f3(S('dark','champ_single','cl',m='lanes_found'),2)} to {f3(S('dark','champ_single',m='lanes_found'),2)} at night.</li>
<li><b>A memory on the input brings most of it back, at no cost on clean frames.</b> The training-free spatial hold lifts the failure half to {f3(S('dark','champ_hold'))} / {f3(S('blur','champ_hold'))} / {f3(S('cam_front3_off','champ_hold'))}; F1@1 gains {bs('dark','champ_hold - champ_single')} at night. With the same hold the champion ties the control on F1 and is higher in S because its graph is sparse.</li>
<li><b>A small learned gate adds a little.</b> A gated memory with 12.5 k parameters, trained out-of-fold on 11 scenes, reaches {f3(S('dark','gate'))} / {f3(S('blur','gate'))} / {f3(S('cam_front3_off','gate'))} (F1@1 against the hold {bs('dark','gate - norec_hold')} at night, {bs('blur','gate - norec_hold')} in blur, {bs('cam_front3_off','gate - norec_hold')} with lost cameras) and lifts the clean half to {f3(S('dark','gate','cl'))}.</li>
<li><b>The builder's own time recursion adds nothing, and fine-tuning the builder on failure frames adds nothing</b> (recursion off: S within 0.01; out-of-fold fine-tune: F1@1 within -0.03 to +0.03, S from +0.01 to -0.04). The missing piece is information, not weights.</li>
<li><b>The navigation attribute is the fragile part.</b> Route success falls from 0.85 on clean frames to 0.14 (night), 0.36 (blur) and 0.35 (three cameras off) and is brought back to only about 0.4, 0.6 and 0.45 by the memory. The cause is that too few lanes are found.</li>
<li><b>The SD map fills most of the gap, if the builder has trained on real failure frames and the map is accurate.</b> A map-conditioned builder trained on real failure frames of the training scenes (E206) with a learned gate in front (E207) reaches failure-half S {f3(S('dark','gateB_m0'))} / {f3(S('blur','gateB_m0'))} / {f3(S('cam_front3_off','gateB_m0'))} (the gated champion: {f3(S('dark','gate'))} / {f3(S('blur','gate'))} / {f3(S('cam_front3_off','gate'))}) and finds {f3(S('dark','gateB_m0',m='lanes_found'),2)} / {f3(S('blur','gateB_m0',m='lanes_found'),2)} / {f3(S('cam_front3_off','gateB_m0',m='lanes_found'),2)} of the lanes; its route success under failure is {rs('e140_route/dark_gateB_B'):.2f} / {rs('e140_route/blur_gateB_B'):.2f} / {rs('e140_route/cam_front3_off_gateB_B'):.2f} against {rs('e135_route/dark_gate'):.2f} / {rs('e135_route/blur_gate'):.2f} / {rs('e135_route/cam_front3_off_gate'):.2f} for the gated champion (clean half {rs('e135_route/dark_single','cl'):.2f}). The map builder trained with synthetic loss of perception only (E204) gained +0.01 to +0.03 on real frames. <b>The map must be good:</b> a registration error of 1 m keeps about half of the benefit, 2 m none (S {f3(S('dark','gateB_m2'))} at night, below {f3(S('dark','gateB_mnone'))} without a map), and a wrong map costs {bs('dark','gateB_mwrong - gateB_mnone')} F1@1 against no map at night; the network does not abstain. The SD map here is simulated from the lane map (loop 7): 'exact' means perfect registration.</li>
<li><b>Joint end-to-end training works mechanically, but gives no measurable gain.</b> The route loss reaches the builder through the node tokens; graph quality stays within 0.004 S, and a control that trains only the route head is as good.</li>
</ul></div>""")

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ chain
    h.append("<h2>1. The chain and what is differentiable</h2>")
    h.append(figure("p17_arch.png", "The robust chain. Blue: learned, green: parameter-free but differentiable, grey dashed: export at inference (the assembly of the beam into a graph; the gradient flows through the kept nodes and their tokens), violet dashed: the gradient path of the route and planner loss. No red blocks: every block is learned or differentiable."))
    h.append("<p>A frame passes the frozen camera + radar foundation (GaussianCaR, 39 BEV channels), the dense head (lane heat and direction, 3 channels) and, new in this loop, a memory stage: the previous fused input, warped by the ego motion, is mixed with the current frame by a gate. The 42 channels feed the builder D7 (1.2 M parameters). Its assembled graph carries node tokens; the route head reads them every 4 m along the edges and cross-attends to the SD-map raster; the consumer predicts the path at 20 m. Time per frame: see section 4.8.</p>")

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ literature
    h.append("<h2>2. Building blocks and literature</h2>")
    h.append("<p>Deep learning as a catalogue of blocks, and which one answers which failure. Three literature agents wrote 103 cards for this loop (cards in <code>report_final/text/lit17/</code>, with the 301 cards of loop 16); they read the method sections through a page digest, not the equations, and mark every link they did not open. The statements below are theirs.</p>")
    h.append(table(["building block", "what it does for us", "evidence in the literature (agent cards)", "tried here"],
                   [["warp + hold / EMA memory on the BEV input", "bridges a failed frame by what was seen before", "temporal fusion is the cheap lever under camera loss: StreamMapNet-style memory +3 to +6 mAP under crash, lost frame, dark, blur in MapBench (2406.12214); memory beyond about 4 frames saturates", "E195 (hold, EMA), E196"],
                    ["gated recurrent write (GRU / Mamba gate)", "keeps a corrupted frame out of the memory ('state contamination')", "SIGMA-Lane (2608.16338), MambaMap (2507.20224); the gated adapter between a frozen fusion and the head of the Post Fusion Stabilizer (2603.05623, 3.3 M parameters, +4.4 mAP at low light, +5.7 ms)", "E199 (12.5 k parameters)"],
                    ["memory of the module's own prediction (query / vertex propagation)", "carries lane structure, not pixels", "StreamMapNet (2308.12570), MapTracker (2403.15951), FASTopoWM (2507.23325); no paper tests it for a lane graph with forks under modality failure", "E196: no effect"],
                    ["training on failures / distillation from a clean teacher", "teaches the head what degraded features mean", "SafeMap (2507.00861): clean-teacher loss on BEV features; MetaBEV (2304.09801): switched-modality training", "E198, E204, E206"],
                    ["adaptive normalisation at test time", "cheap adaptation to night", "AdaBN / TENT can collapse at batch size 1 (agent B, from the cards of 2411.18860); +0.04 seen in loop 5", "not repeated"],
                    ["cross-attention to a map (SD map tokens)", "assigns the route to lanes, and could add lanes", "NavMapFusion (2512.03317): shift noise 1 m holds to 3 m, 10 % wrong maps limit the drop; UMPE (2605.02762): missing map as a trained mode; ONR / MAT (2507.07487) closest to our route head", "route head (loop 16b), E204, E206"],
                    ["matching with a dustbin (SuperGlue 1911.11763, LightGlue 2306.13643)", "an abstain output for a wrong or missing map", "no paper tests a planner against a wrong route (agent C)", "not built: open"],
                    ["joint training through the node tokens", "the route or planner loss shapes the builder", "route-as-lane-mask planners (GC-PGP 2302.07753, Diffusion Planner 2501.15564); shortcut risk documented (Hidden Biases 2306.07957)", "E202"]]))

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ protocol
    h.append("<h2>3. Protocol and its limits</h2>")
    h.append("<ul><li><b>Failure series.</b> 22 validation scenes, 291 frames per failure type, every third key frame (1.5 s apart). The first half of a scene is clean, the second half uses the perturbed foundation features of one failure type (protocol of loops 5 to 14). Each cell below has 137 clean-half and 154 failure-half frames.</li><li><b>Metrics.</b> The loop-16 composite S (F1 at 1 m and 0.5 m, junction F1, sparsity, false length) at the champion's fixed threshold and assembly; paired scene bootstrap (2000 draws, 22 scenes) for F1@1 differences. Route success against the ground-truth route points, two route-head seeds (seed noise up to 0.03).</li><li><b>What was not touched.</b> The test frames. Nothing on the failure series was selected by threshold or settings; learned parts (gate, fine-tune, map builder) were trained on the training scenes or out-of-fold on the other half of the validation scenes.</li><li><b>Limits.</b> Eleven training scenes per fold are few. A failure lasts half a scene; real failures start and end differently. The perturbations are synthetic images and dropped sensors, not recorded night drives. Failures are scored with the clean-time threshold. One dataset, one city set (the splits share places).</li></ul>")

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ results
    h.append("<h2>4. Experiments</h2>")
    h.append("<h3>4.1 E193: what a failure costs the champion and the control</h3>")
    h.append("<p><b>Hypothesis.</b> Both chains read the same 42 channels, so the champion loses as much as the control. <b>Setup.</b> Single frame, failure series, control = E94 graphs of loops 13 / 14 on the same frames. <b>Result.</b> Confirmed. The loss is a loss of lanes found (0.10 at night against 0.71 on the clean half); the graph that is found is as accurate as before, so sparse graphs fail by absence, not by false lanes.</p>")
    for p in PERT3:
        h.append(f"<h3 style='font-size:9pt'>{esc(NAME[p])}</h3>" + g["tbl_main"](p, ["ctrl_single", "champ_single"], ref={"champ_single": "ctrl_single"}))
    h.append("<h3>4.2 E194: four milder failure types</h3>")
    h.append(g["tbl_more"]())
    h.append("<p>Fog, radar off and one front camera off cost 0.04 to 0.08 S; an extrinsics error costs 0.13 and is not repaired by memory (J falls with the hold, 0.25 to 0.12; the reason is not isolated). Night and blur are the hard cases.</p>")
    h.append("<h3>4.3 E195 / E196: memory on the input, and the builder's own recursion</h3>")
    h.append("<p><b>Hypothesis.</b> Most of the loss is lost input, so a memory in front of the builder repairs it; the builder's time recursion (prior from the previous frame's graph) should help too. <b>Design.</b> Spatial hold: per pixel the decayed (0.95), ego-motion-warped previous input replaces the current frame where its lane heat is higher. EMA 0.5 with a label-free heat monitor as the second variant. Both are parameter-free and differentiable (warp = grid_sample). <b>Result.</b> The hold confirms the first hypothesis and costs nothing on clean frames; the recursion is not confirmed: with it off the failure half changes by 0.00 to 0.01 S.</p>")
    for p in PERT3:
        h.append(f"<h3 style='font-size:9pt'>{esc(NAME[p])}</h3>" + g["tbl_main"](p, ["ctrl_hold", "champ_single", "champ_hold", "champ_ema", "norec_single", "norec_hold"], ref={"champ_hold": "champ_single", "champ_ema": "champ_single", "norec_hold": "champ_hold"}))
    h.append(figure("p17_summary.png", "Left to right, top to bottom: (1) failure-half S by failure type and system, with the clean half as the dashed line; (2) route success under failure; (3) the map builder on synthetic loss of perception; (4) the map builder on real failure frames.", 96))
    h.append("<h3>4.4 E199: a learned gated memory</h3>")
    h.append("<p><b>Hypothesis.</b> A learned gate beats the training-free hold, because it can see when the current frame is bad and when the memory is old. <b>Architecture.</b> The memory y(t-1) is warped by the ego motion. A small conv net (11 input channels: heat and direction of the frame and of the warped memory, the maxdecay decision, validity, a feature-mismatch map and two feature-energy maps; 3 convolutions, 12.5 k parameters) outputs two gates, one for the 39 feature channels and one for heat / direction; y = g * memory + (1 - g) * frame. The gate starts as the hold (checked: it reproduces it to within 1 % of the signal), the builder is frozen, the loss is the builder loss of frame t, three frames are unrolled with the memory detached before the first. Training: 1500 steps (12 minutes) on failure and clean frames of the scenes of the other fold. <b>Result.</b> Confirmed, small.</p>")
    for p in PERT3:
        h.append(f"<h3 style='font-size:9pt'>{esc(NAME[p])}</h3>" + g["tbl_main"](p, ["norec_single", "norec_hold", "gate", "ctrl_hold"], ref={"norec_hold": "norec_single", "gate": "norec_hold", "ctrl_hold": "norec_single"}))
    h.append(figure("p17_frames_dark.png", "Night, failure half. Columns: frames at the 10th / 35th / 65th / 90th percentile of the per-frame F1@1 difference between gate and single frame (selected by the number, not by looks). Rows: ground truth (green band), single frame, spatial hold, learned gate, control with hold.", 78))
    h.append(figure("p17_frames_blur.png", "Motion blur, the same selection rule.", 78))
    h.append("<h3>4.5 E133: failure-trained input stage and failure-frame fine-tuning</h3>")
    h.append("<p><b>E197.</b> The dense head of loop 5 trained on perturbed training frames (e65_ftall) as the input stage: single frame slightly better, no better with the hold (the heat does not drop, so the monitor never fires). <b>E198.</b> The builder fine-tuned 1.5 u on half clean training frames, half failure-half frames of the other fold's scenes: no gain out-of-fold. <b>Conclusion.</b> About 80 failure frames per type and fold do not move the builder; the lanes are not in the input.</p>")
    for p in PERT3:
        h.append(f"<h3 style='font-size:9pt'>{esc(NAME[p])}</h3>" + g["tbl_main"](p, ["champ_single", "ftall_single", "ft_single", "champ_hold", "ftall_hold", "ft_hold"], ref={"ftall_single": "champ_single", "ft_single": "champ_single", "ftall_hold": "champ_hold", "ft_hold": "champ_hold"}))
    h.append("<h3>4.6 E200: map assignment under failure</h3>")
    h.append("<p>The route head along the edges (two seeds) on the graphs of the series, SD map without error and with a scene-constant pose error of 2 m. Route success falls much further than the graph score: a lane that is not found cannot carry the route.</p>" + g["tbl_route"]())
    h.append("<h3>4.7 E204 / E206: does the SD map fill what perception lost?</h3>")
    h.append("<p><b>Hypothesis.</b> A builder that sees the SD map as five extra input channels can add lanes where the perception is blind. <b>Design.</b> The first stem convolution is widened (new weights zero, so the network starts as the champion); training shows the network a map with pose error 0 to 3 m, a wrong map (10 %) or no map (10 %), and removes the perception in 40 % of the frames on purpose (global attenuation of heat, direction and features, or rectangles with no evidence). <b>E204 result.</b> On the real failure series the gain is small and mostly independent of the map:</p>" + g["tbl_map"]())
    h.append("<p><b>Diagnosis (E205).</b> On the validation frames with the same synthetic loss as in training the picture is different: the champion falls to S 0.463 (lanes found 0.16), the map builder reaches 0.678 without a map (0.56 found), 0.700 with an exact map (0.69 found), 0.672 with a 2 m error and 0.646 with a wrong map. So the training with degraded inputs gives most of the gain; the exact map adds 0.022; a wrong map costs 0.032 against no map. And nothing of this transfers to real failure frames: the synthetic loss is not the real one.</p>")
    if g["has_e139"]:
        h.append(g["e139_html"]())
    h.append("<h3>4.8 E202: joint end-to-end fine-tune</h3>")
    h.append("<p><b>Design.</b> Builder (trainable) -> beam assembly (discrete: it decides which nodes and edges exist) -> the builder's node tokens gathered at the surviving vertices and interpolated along the edges by a fixed sparse matrix -> route head (trainable, cross-attention to the SD raster) -> route label per point. The route loss therefore reaches the builder. Arms: a = route loss + builder loss (weight 1), b = route loss weighted 20 times higher, c = control as b, but the tokens are detached so only the route head learns. 600 iterations, batch 4, from the champion and the route head of seed 0; map faults as in the route-head training. <b>Result.</b> The gradient arrives (norm 6.7 in arm a) but the route loss on training frames is only 0.03, because the route head already fits them. Route success (seed 0, exact map, one value per cell, about 137 frames in a clean half):</p>")
    rows = []
    for nm, tag in (("base: champion + route head seed 0", "base"), ("a: joint, builder loss weight 1", "a"), ("b: joint, route loss x20", "b"), ("c: control, route loss does not reach the builder", "c")):
        r = [esc(nm)]
        for series in ("dark_single", "dark_maxdecay_0.95", "blur_maxdecay_0.95"):
            c = MJ["route"].get(f"e136_route/{series}_{tag}", {})
            for ph in ("cl", "fail"):
                xs = [v["route_success"] for k, v in c.items() if k.endswith(f"_{ph}")]
                r.append(f3(xs[0]) if xs else "-")
        rows.append(r)
    h.append(table(["arm", "dark single: clean", "failure", "dark hold: clean", "failure", "blur hold: clean", "failure"], rows, nums=set(range(1, 7))))
    h.append("<p>Continued training of the route head (arm c) is as good as, or better than, the joint arms; the gain over the base is the extra training of the head, not the gradient into the builder. Graph quality is unchanged (clean S 0.746 to 0.750, failure S within 0.004). One seed, a standard error of about 0.03: the experiment cannot show an effect smaller than that.</p>")
    h.append("<h3>4.9 Time per frame</h3>")
    h.append("<p>Median over 60 validation frames, batch 1, idle RTX 3060, cached foundation features (not timed, the same for every system), CUDA graphs for the builder and the route head. The memory stage is the warp of the 42 channels and the three convolutions of the gate.</p>" + g["tbl_latency"]())

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ understanding
    h.append("<h2>5. Where it falls short, and why</h2>")
    h.append("<ul><li><b>Lanes found, not lane quality.</b> After the memory the failure half still finds 0.43 to 0.50 of the lanes (0.71 to 0.74 on the clean half). F1@1 of what is found is 0.70 to 0.73. Lanes that the vehicle drives into during the failure are in no earlier frame and in no feature.</li><li><b>Route success follows lanes found.</b> It needs the lane the route runs on. 0.4 to 0.6 against 0.85.</li><li><b>Junctions.</b> J falls to 0.15 to 0.19 (0.25 clean) and the hold lowers it a little on the clean half too (reason not isolated).</li><li><b>Extrinsics.</b> A calibration error stays in every held frame. The literature has no downstream-only fix (agent B).</li><li><b>Synthetic is not real.</b> Training on synthetic loss of perception gave +0.2 S on synthetic frames and +0.015 on real ones; only real failure frames in the training (E206) transferred.</li><li><b>The map is the new dependency.</b> With the map the failure half comes within about 0.08 of the clean half in S; the benefit needs a registration error below about 1 to 2 m, and a wrong map is worse than no map. A chain that depends on the map needs a trust signal; the label-free agreement of loop 8 fails at night.</li><li><b>Three cameras off with the hold.</b> The hold lowers the route success of the map builder (see section 4.7): memory of lanes behind the vehicle does not carry the lane ahead, and the single frame already has the map.</li></ul>")
    h.append("<h2>6. Best method so far, and what is open</h2>")
    h.append(f"<div class='box'><p><b>Best chain without a map.</b> Champion builder + frozen foundation and dense head + <b>learned gated memory on the input</b> (12.5 k parameters, starts as the spatial hold) + route head along the edges + consumer. Time recursion off (no effect, one builder pass less). Failure-half S {f3(S('dark','gate'))} / {f3(S('blur','gate'))} / {f3(S('cam_front3_off','gate'))} (night / blur / three cameras off) against {f3(S('dark','norec_single'))} / {f3(S('blur','norec_single'))} / {f3(S('cam_front3_off','norec_single'))} without memory and {f3(S('dark','gate','cl'))} on clean frames; route success {rs('e135_route/dark_gate'):.2f} / {rs('e135_route/blur_gate'):.2f} / {rs('e135_route/cam_front3_off_gate'):.2f}.</p><p><b>Best chain with an accurate SD map (registration error below about 1 m).</b> The same chain with the map-conditioned builder B, trained on real failure frames, behind the gate. Failure-half S {f3(S('dark','gateB_m0'))} / {f3(S('blur','gateB_m0'))} / {f3(S('cam_front3_off','gateB_m0'))}, route success {rs('e140_route/dark_gateB_B'):.2f} / {rs('e140_route/blur_gateB_B'):.2f} / {rs('e140_route/cam_front3_off_gateB_B'):.2f}, clean half S {f3(S('dark','gateB_m0','cl'))}; about {g['latency_total']} per frame. It needs a trust signal for the map before it can be used without a safety net.</p>" + figure("p17_best.png", "The two best chains against the champion, for the three main failure types. Left: failure-half S. Right: route success.", 96) + "<p><b>Open, in this order.</b> (1) A trust signal for the SD map: the network does not abstain, a wrong map costs about 0.05 F1@1 against no map and a 2 m error removes the benefit. (2) More real failure frames and scenes for the builder and the gate (the training saw 842 rows per type; the gate 11 scenes per fold). (3) A TEST run of the route head along the edges, the learned gate and the map builder: needs your decision; TEST has been used once in loop 16. (4) Radar-only lane evidence as an extra input under camera failure. (5) A real, registered navigation map instead of the map simulated from the lane map.</p></div>")
    h.append("<h2>7. Constraints and limits, in short</h2>")
    h.append("<ul><li>Validation scenes only; test untouched.</li><li>22 scenes, 154 failure frames per cell: differences below 0.01 S are noise.</li><li>Seed noise of the route head up to 0.03.</li><li>Learned parts see 11 scenes per fold (gate, fine-tune).</li><li>Failures are synthetic and last half a scene.</li><li>The literature statements are from page digests, not read at equation level.</li><li>One GPU (RTX 3060): three jobs at a time.</li></ul>")
    h.append("<h2>Appendix: experiments and files</h2>")
    h.append(table(["id", "what", "script", "result file"],
                   [["E193 / E194", "champion on the failure series, seven types", "p17_series.py, p17_eval.py", "e17/e130_champion, e130b_more"],
                    ["E195", "spatial hold, EMA + monitor hold", "p17_eval.py", "e17/e131_hold"],
                    ["E196", "builder recursion off", "p17_eval.py --prev 0", "e17/e132_norec"],
                    ["E197 / b", "failure-trained dense head; failure-frame fine-tune, two folds", "p17_dense.py, p17_ft.py, p17_merge.py", "e17/e133a_ftall, e133b_k0 / k1"],
                    ["E199", "learned gated memory, two folds", "p17_gate.py", "e17/e134_gate"],
                    ["E200", "route success on the series", "p17_route.py", "e17/e135_route"],
                    ["E202", "joint end-to-end fine-tune, three arms", "p17_joint.py", "e17/e136_route, e136_graph_*"],
                    ["E203", "time per frame", "p17_latency.py", "e17/latency"],
                    ["E204 / E205 / E206", "map-conditioned builder", "p17_mapnet.py, p17_mapft.py, p17_mapdiag.py, p17_dense_train.py", "e17/e138_map, e139_b, e139_c, e138b_mapdiag.json"],
                    ["numbers", "every number of this report", "p17_master.py", "e17/results_master.json"]]))
    return h
